<title>HONG KONG: Trade in Pacific Concord shrs suspended.</title>
<headline>Trade in Pacific Concord shrs suspended.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in the shares of Pacific Concord Holdings Ltd was suspended on Wednesday at the company's request pending an announcement, the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong said.  </p>
<p>Pacific Concord shares closed at HK$3.45, down HK$0.025 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company announced on Tuesday it would pay HK$134 million for 196.4 million shares of Yaohan International Holdings Ltd from Kazuo Wada, chairman of Yaohan Group, and his family.</p>
<p>The deal was the first step in forming a strategic alliance between Pacific Concord and Yaohan Group involving active cooperation in developing and operating department stores, megamarts and supermarkets in China, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
